refs.append(dict(id='minor2022',title='Fixed-Parameter Tractability of Graph Isomorphism in Graphs with an Excluded Minor',authors='Daniel Lokshtanov; Marcin Pilipczuk; Michał Pilipczuk; Saket Saurabh',year=2022,url='https://doi.org/10.1145/3519935.3520076',pdf_url='https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10477129',locator='STOC 2022, pp. 914–923, Theorem 1.1 and the paragraph immediately following it: one uniform algorithm, but the parameter-dependent time bound is not proved computable. Full-version record: arXiv:2210.14638.'))
save(i,dict(title='Graph isomorphism parameterized by vertex deletion to planarity',formal='Is there one deterministic algorithm A, a total computable function f:N→N, and an absolute constant c such that, for every h≥0 and every pair of finite simple undirected graphs G₁,G₂ that can each be made planar by deleting at most h vertices, A decides whether G₁≅G₂ in at most f(h)(n+1)^c steps, where n=|V(G₁)|+|V(G₂)|? The input consists of the graphs and h; deletion sets and planar embeddings are not supplied. This uses the usual effective definition of fixed-parameter tractability, including computability of f.',definitions='For a graph G and X⊆V(G), G−X is the induced graph obtained by deleting X and its incident edges. A graph is planar if it can be drawn in the plane with edges intersecting only at common endpoints. Put a(G)=min{|X|:G−X is planar} and G_h={G:a(G)≤h}. The graphs may be disconnected and have no vertex colors or edge weights. They are encoded by adjacency matrices on numbered vertices; h is a binary integer, and it suffices to consider 0≤h≤n, as larger h can be capped. An isomorphism is a bijection φ:V(G₁)→V(G₂) with {u,v}∈E(G₁) exactly when {φ(u),φ(v)}∈E(G₂). The required output is yes or no, with no error. The algorithm is a uniform deterministic Turing algorithm: one finite program handles all h, and f must be computable by a terminating program on every integer input. The polynomial exponent c is independent of h. The displayed correctness and time guarantees concern promised pairs in G_h; recognition or producing a deletion set is not a separate required output. This parameter is vertex deletion distance to planarity, not Euler genus, edge deletion distance, or an iterated elimination distance.',question_type='yes_no',answer_criterion='Prove or refute the existence of the stated uniform algorithm with a computable parameter bound f and an exponent independent of h. An n^{O(h)} algorithm, a separate polynomial-time algorithm for each fixed h with no uniform computable bound, or a bound f(h)n^c whose f is not shown computable does not establish this effective FPT target.',context_blocks=[dict(title='A small exceptional vertex set need not have a prescribed image',text='After removing at most h vertices, both graphs become planar. Isomorphism must nevertheless respect the full graphs, including all edges incident to those vertices. The question asks for a polynomial exponent independent of their number.',citation='primary'),dict(title='The source result covers a different structural parameter',text='The 2021 paper supplies an FPT isomorphism test for graphs excluding K_{3,t} as a minor, including bounded-genus graphs. It separately defines G_h by vertex deletion to planarity and asks about FPT on this class.',citation='primary'),dict(title='The 2022 result nearly answers the question',text='The STOC 2022 theorem gives one algorithm for H-minor-free graphs with time g(H)n^{O(1)}, but explicitly states that g is not guaranteed computable. Its authors note that this falls outside the usual definition of FPT. As a direct class-containment consequence, it also gives a bound depending only on h for G_h: such a graph excludes K_{h+5} as a minor. This consequence retains the same computability caveat.',citation='minor2022'),dict(title='What remains under the stated interpretation',text='The card preserves standard effective FPT as the target. If arbitrary, possibly noncomputable parameter dependence was all that was intended, the 2022 theorem supplies a positive answer to that relaxed reading. It is therefore no longer accurate to describe the question without recording that progress.',citation='minor2022')],why='Would show that graph isomorphism retains an effective fixed-parameter running-time guarantee under a bounded number of arbitrary vertex additions to a planar graph.',references=refs,progress=[dict(date='2021',text='The source asks for FPT isomorphism on graphs made planar by deleting at most h vertices.',citation='primary'),dict(date='2022-06',text='A uniform canonization theorem for excluded-minor graphs yields an h-dependent polynomial bound for this class, with the explicit caveat that its parameter function need not be computable.',citation='minor2022')],status='source_open',status_note='The broad fixed-parameter-shaped bound follows from the 2022 excluded-minor theorem; its proof statement expressly does not guarantee a computable parameter function. The card asks for the usual effective FPT guarantee. Checked the full published theorem and subsequent searches through 12 September 2026; no result removing this caveat for G_h was identified.',model_self_contained=True,requires_context=False,importance=dict(score=c['importance']['score'],method='editorial',reason='A structural extension of planar isomorphism whose remaining effective parameter dependence is mathematically distinct from an arbitrary parameter-dependent bound. Existing score retained.',assessed_on=DATE),review_note='Defined G_h, the graph-isomorphism decision task and all FPT quantifiers. Added the 2022 excluded-minor advance and its explicit effectiveness caveat; did not report the relaxed result as a complete solution of standard FPT.',working_summary=dict(sentences=['Each input graph becomes planar after deleting at most h vertices.','The algorithm must decide whether the full graphs are isomorphic, without being given deletion sets or embeddings.','The target is time f(h)n^c for one deterministic algorithm, a computable f and an exponent c independent of h.','A 2022 excluded-minor theorem already supplies the shape of this bound but does not establish that its parameter function is computable.','The remaining question under the usual FPT convention is an effective bound, rather than polynomial time for each separately fixed h.'],basis='saved_sources',source_basis='source-text',written_on=DATE,source_refs=['primary','minor2022'])),notes=['Recovered G_h as vertex deletion distance to planarity.','Defined input promises, isomorphism, deterministic uniformity and effective FPT quantifiers.','Checked the 2022 excluded-minor theorem and transferred its stated bound with the computability caveat intact.','Distinguished the relaxed reading already answered from the standard effective target.'],checked_sources=[r['url'] for r in refs]+['https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.14638','https://acm-stoc.org/stoc2022/accepted-papers.html'])
